WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.280
He always promised he would be back.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:07.430
Terminator star Arnold Schwarzenegger and
original Sarah Connor actor Linda Hamilton

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:12.330
are back in action in a batch of new photos
from the upcoming sci-fi sequel, Terminator:

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.660
Dark Fate.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.011
One new photo released by the studio shows
a grizzled and bearded Schwarzenegger, as

00:00:18.011 --> 00:00:23.010
the T-800 model Terminator, sporting a scar
and giving the stink-eye to someone off camera.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:27.730
Another depicts Hamilton in character as Sarah
Connor, looking older but no less battle-hardened

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.289
with a heavy vest of armor on her chest, and
aviator sunglasses.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:35.970
Though Terminator: Dark Fate does feature
the two iconic franchise stars, it also brings

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.500
several new faces into the fold: Mackenzie
Davis as a soldier-assassin named Grace, Natalia

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:48.620
Reyes as Dani Ramos , Diego Boneta as Miguel
Ramos, and Gabriel Luna as a new type of Terminator.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.620
IGN shared stills of each star new to the
series in action, with shots including

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.370
Davis' Grace character staring down an opponent
mid-fight,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:02.190
Reyes' Dani peeking over her shoulder near
a parked car in the middle of an open field,

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.620
Boneta's Miguel affecting a scowl from behind
the wheel of a truck,

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.880
and Luna's Terminator dressed in what looks
to be a military uniform while stalking through

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.920
some sort of high-tech facility.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.780
Set after the events of T2: Judgment Day,
Dark Fate will effectively do to the Terminator

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.720
franchise what 2018's Halloween revival did
with its own series - by pretending most of

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.920
the sequels in the series didn't happen.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.220
Instead, Dark Fate is reportedly picking up
at the last point basically everyone agreed

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.670
the series was still good.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.840
As a result, the movie won't address the events
of 2003's Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines,

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:41.590
2009's Terminator Salvation, or 2015's much-maligned
Terminator Genisys - likely for the better.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.590
As producer David Ellison once said of the
film's focus,

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:49.380
"I will say we have resolved the future of
the franchise, and believe me, it's an incredibly

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.420
bright future.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:55.031
I think where it's going will be the continuation
of what the fans really wanted since T2 … It's

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:59.060
something we're incredibly excited about and
we think is the direction it needs to head."

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:03.479
James Cameron, the director and writer of
the first two films and a longtime series

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:08.090
producer, is also back in the creative mix
for Dark Fate, and he's previously shared

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:11.340
his vision for this transformative sixth movie
in the franchise.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.780
Speaking in an interview in July 2017, Cameron
expressed that the goal with the forthcoming

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.010
movie is to pass the narrative baton through
the introduction of new characters, while

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.900
also modernizing the doomsday narrative to
reflect current technological anxieties.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.480
He's also aware that the franchise needs a
careful approach to bring it back in line

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.890
with the speculative sci-fi ambitions of the
first two movies.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.070
As Cameron phrased it,

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.900
"The question is, 'Has the franchise run its
course or can it be freshened up?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.870
Can it still have relevance now, where so
much of our world is catching up to what was

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.810
science fiction in the first two films?'"

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:47.220
Despite how important the new characters may
be for evolving and continuing the Terminator

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.880
series, Dark Fate director Tim Miller says
that Linda Hamilton is the most vital piece

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.050
of this movie's puzzle.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:57.380
He explained to IGN that Hamilton returning
to her role as Sarah Connor made a vision

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.450
for the new sequel fall into place for him,
and that her presence helps bridge the gap

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.160
between past franchise entries and installments
that are yet to come.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.400
"You think you're safe and alive?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.080
You're already dead.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.560
Everybody.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.560
Him, you - you're dead already."

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:17.080
The director said, "The fact that Linda came
back makes this particular Terminator fresh.

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:19.960
This story could only continue with her in
the role of Sarah Connor.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.910
That's the most important thing for me.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.430
Linda reinvented this character in a way that
both honors who she was before and brings

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.730
something new to the role."

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:32.270
He also gave major kudos to the new cast,
all of whom he says hold their own and bring

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.620
something new to the table while sharing the
screen with Hamilton and Schwarzenegger.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:41.690
Miller also teased the movie's focus on character
over big-budget spectacle, investing audiences

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.590
in the cast before putting them all in peril.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.590
He said,

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:48.600
"We have a lot of powerful, moving character
moments up front, but toward the back half

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.640
of the movie, when s--- gets going [...] it
just doesn't stop.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.909
And we tried very hard to make it all different
and fresh - it's not just people punching

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:59.209
each other; it's a roller coaster ride and
I think [it's] great."

00:03:59.209 --> 00:04:03.690
Fans can watch as old-school meets new-school
when Terminator: Dark Fate arrives in theaters

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.890
on November 1.

